From a0a17a83d18f338d0e18febdbc3f71f53a03f6ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:37:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] audit pass: private temp files, permission heals, a strlcpy,
 three removals

From the 2026-11-05 Audit Findings pass:
- httpd: login_url is copied with strlcpy.
- WireGuard writes its route and script temp files in root's 0700 /tmp/reaper, not the shared
  /tmp.
- rwatch takes write-for-everyone off nt_center.pid, netool.pid and the diag databases on each
  tick (closed programs write them 0666), and the Security Review scans a USB long-term store as
  well as /jffs.
- A USB long-term store gets the same no-follow permission sweep /jffs gets at boot when it
  appears; the walk is handed the store's base path alone.
- wallguardc reads at most 2 MiB of a list. lighttpd links with full RELRO.
- Removed: the wlcsm_bindfix shim (each model's own libnvram.so and libwlcsm.so already carry the
  socket-leak fix), lld2d / lld2c (never started), and the AFP DHX1 login module (DHX2 stays).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
